waydroid-host-stack: devices heard in the discovery announced every second.

The discovery loop seeds the guest with BlueZ's known devices only when
discovery starts; after that it forwards a device only on DeviceAdded,
which discover_devices_with_changes emits on property changes.  A guest
scan that starts while discovery already runs gets no seed, and a steady
advertiser changes nothing: the controller filters duplicates until its
LE scan restarts (about every 34 s in BlueZ's dual discovery on the
Pro1x's WCN3990) and BlueZ emits no RSSI equal to the last one.  The
parked car reached Android once every 34 s, none inside the Tesla app's
10 s scans, "no_peripherals" (Pro1x, 2026-11-27).  Each second, every
device with an RSSI (BlueZ keeps one only for devices heard in the
current discovery and clears them when it stops) goes again to the
matching sessions.  Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix, 2026-11-27), on d9a316e
(MIT), after waydroid-host-stack-scan-duplicate-data.patch.

